%% Human-in-the-loop remediation
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor R as Requester
  actor IC as Incident commander
  actor O as Service owner
  participant E as remediation.Engine
  participant TL as Timeline (hash-chained)
  participant K as Kubernetes
  R->>E: run k8s.rollout_undo … (or click triage suggestion)
  E->>E: catalog lookup · param schema · allowed scopes
  E->>K: DryRun (read-only, client-side diff)
  E->>TL: action_requested · action_dry_run
  E-->>R: approval card (diff, risk=high, expiry 15 min)
  R->>E: Approve
  E-->>R: refused: requester cannot approve
  IC->>E: Approve
  E->>TL: action_approved (role=ic)
  O->>E: Approve
  E->>TL: action_approved (role=service_owner)
  E->>TL: re-read + verify hash chain, rebuild approvals
  alt approvals in timeline do not satisfy policy
    E-->>O: refuse to execute
  else kill switch off (env REMEDIATION_ENABLED or DB flag)
    E->>TL: note: dry-run only
    E-->>O: approved, no change made (manual steps shown)
  else both keys on
    E->>K: Execute (patch / scale)
    E->>K: Verify rollout
    E->>TL: action_executed · action_verified
  end
